* Behavioural operational amplifier: one pole, finite gain, output resistance and
* output swing.
* aol: open-loop DC gain; gbw: gain-bandwidth product [Hz]; rout: output resistance
* [ohm]; vsat: the output saturates at +-vsat [V].
* Without the limit, a fault that makes a filter unstable would give a response that
* grows without bound; a real amplifier stops at its supply rails.
* No slew-rate limit and no offset.
.subckt opamp inp inn out aol=2e5 gbw=1e7 rout=50 vsat=12
Gm 0 n1 inp inn 1m
Rp n1 0 {aol*1k}
Cp n1 0 {1m/(6.283185307*gbw)}
Bsat n1 0 I = v(n1) > {vsat} ? v(n1)-{vsat} : (v(n1) < -{vsat} ? v(n1)+{vsat} : 0)
Eo n2 0 n1 0 1
Ro n2 out {rout}
.ends opamp
